{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And you shall call out to it for peace.</b> For great is peace, that the Holy One, blessed be He, altered [the truth] when Sarah said, ״ואדני זקן״, and likewise it is written ״חבור עצבים אפרים הנח לו״, as Rashi explained above. And moreover, how many quills are broken, how much ink is spilled, for אחי יוסף אביך צוה לפני מותו לאמר כה תאמרון ליוסף וגו׳ — and we do not find that Jacob so commanded; rather, only for the sake of peace did He write it. And also the priestly blessing concludes with peace, and likewise the Shemoneh Esreh. And further, our Rabbis taught: one asks after the peace of gentiles מפני דרכי שלום. And also one who anticipates another with peace — must repeat it back to him: ״לשלום״, and to him: ״לו שלום עליך וברכה טובה.״ And they support this language from what is written: ״כי תקדמנו ברכות טוב״ — meaning, if he anticipates you with peace, you must return to him a good blessing. Therefore said Rabbi Yochanan: No person ever anticipated me with peace — even a gentile in the marketplace, where it is not customary to hurry so much and to anticipate him with peace — but I anticipated him, because if he were to anticipate me, I would have to repeat the peace back to him, and one does not repeat peace to a gentile. And further, our Rabbis said: finding a deaf-mute, an imbecile, or a minor — there is robbery in them, מפני דרכי שלום. And likewise one sustains the poor of gentiles along with the poor of Israel מפני דרכי שלום. And therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, blessed His people with peace, as it is said: ״ה׳ יברך את עמו בשלום״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:10.418986510Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}